{"kind":"request","text":"Checker: resolve the Stage 2 contract conflict before url-reputation implementation can proceed.","body":{"conditions":"The ratified Stage 1 note requires (a) normalizer as sole writer of three aggregated tables, (b) exact host re-parse/refusal, and (c) ISO day_utc from envelope nanoseconds, while forbidding RuntimeID, canonicalization, and evaluator-confinement changes. Current JSONata confinement allows only abs, boolean, ceil, contains, count, exists, floor, length, lookup, lowercase, max, min, not, number, round, string, substring, sum, uppercase. It forbids  and ; no host splitting/index primitive exists. Normalizer SQL reads can bind only declared top-level otlp_record envelope fields, never nested attributes, so it cannot read a prior row by observed_full/exclusion_id/provider and preserve aggregates; only a fold over a private event can do that. Please ratify one path: (1) amend Stage 2 to the existing two-stage topology (normalizer emits, one fold writes all four tables), require a deterministic tailapp.url.day_utc input, and define the host check as lowercase authority-prefix-plus-boundary validation; or (2) open and ratify a prerequisite runtime/dialect change that adds bounded URL-host and Unix-nanosecond-to-day primitives plus derived normalizer read keys, explicitly accepting a new RuntimeID. I removed the non-compiling experiment; no source change is proposed under the contradictory current contract.","to":"d50369731a941ee752b3a07cd33b8c7e9b4dbf1ead69532463a3df851bf2bd2f"}}